        "original_id": "d106e874-7c1a-59a2-9504-5865fb4a5bf6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Awki, Jacabamba, Andes, South America\n- Topics: mountain ranges, glaciers, climatic regimes\n- Countries: Venezuela, Colombia, Ecuador, Peru, Bolivia, Argentina, Chile\n\nFacts:\n- Awki lies southeast of Jacabamba.\n- The Andes, also called the Andean Mountains or Spanish \"Cordillera de los Andes,\" are the longest continental mountain range in the world.\n- The Andes extend north to south through Venezuela, Colombia, Ecuador, Peru, Bolivia, Argentina, and Chile.\n- Glaciers in South America develop exclusively on the Andes.\n- Glaciers in South America are subject to the Andes climatic regimes of the Tropical Andes, Dry Andes, and Wet Andes.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
